==============================================================================
(1) WHAT EACH READING PREDICTS
==============================================================================
  ACCUMULATED:  N = 3.82e+05 turns  ->  f_bar = 2/pi to within 8.33e-05%
                 2/pi is PREDICTED. No freedom, nothing to fit.

  INSTANTANEOUS: f_bar = |cos theta_freeze|, drawn once from the |cos| distribution,
                 whose density is 2/(pi sqrt(1-x^2)) on [0,1] and whose MEAN is 2/pi --
                 so 2/pi is the typical value but carries the full spread.
                 spread: sd(|cos|) = sqrt(1/2 - (2/pi)^2) = 0.3078  (48.3% of the mean)

==============================================================================
(2) THE CORPUS'S TWO MEASUREMENTS, AGAINST BOTH
==============================================================================
  measurement          value   offset from 2/pi   P(frozen lands this close)
  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  fit-implied         0.6253              1.78%                        1.87%
  winding-sim         0.6350              0.25%                        0.27%

  Under the accumulated reading each of these is a hit with probability ~1 (the
  prediction is 2/pi and the measurements carry their own errors).
  Under the instantaneous reading each is a coincidence at the quoted probability.

==============================================================================
(3) THE LIKELIHOOD RATIO
==============================================================================
  ONLY ONE of the two measurements may be used, and it is not the tighter one.
  The winding-sim SIMULATES the winding premise, so it is guaranteed to land on 2/pi
  whatever the physical window is -- it tests the arithmetic of the average, not the
  choice of window. Quoting its 0.25% as evidence against the frozen reading would be
  circular. The fit-implied value is the only number drawn from data rather than from
  the premise under test.

    fit-implied f_bar = 0.6253, offset 1.78%
    P(a frozen phase lands this close to 2/pi) = 1.87%
    odds favouring the accumulated reading      = 54 : 1

  That is modest evidence, and it should be read as modest. A 1-in-53 coincidence is
  not rare across a corpus with far more than 53 numbers in it, so the look-elsewhere
  effect eats much of it. What it is NOT vulnerable to is fitting: the turn budget was
  computed from theta_dot/H = 2.4e6 and theta_dot ~ T^3, both recorded for baryogenesis
  and neither touched by the amplitude, so 3.82e5 turns was not chosen to make this work.

==============================================================================
(4) THE SENSITIVITY — HOW CLOSE WOULD IT HAVE TO BE TO SETTLE IT?
==============================================================================
    offset from 2/pi    P(frozen)         odds
  ----------------------------------------------
              10.00%      10.548%           9:1
               5.00%       5.260%          19:1
               2.00%       2.102%          48:1
               1.81%       1.903%          53:1
               1.00%       1.051%          95:1
               0.30%       0.315%         317:1
               0.10%       0.105%         951:1

  The corpus's tightest reading sits at 1.81%. Halving the measurement error would
  roughly double the odds; getting to 0.3% would put it past 300:1. So this is a
  question the production chains can actually settle, and the quantity to watch is the
  posterior width on epsilon, since f_bar is inferred through it.

==============================================================================
VERDICT
==============================================================================
  The window is the ACCUMULATED one, at evidence grade rather than by assertion. The
  distinction matters beyond bookkeeping because the two readings differ in KIND:

    * accumulated -> f_bar = 2/pi is a theorem given the turn budget, the alpha_c
      conflict stands at its full 2.08%, and branch (a) of that conflict is dead by
      six orders. Nothing about f_bar is available to relieve the tension.
    * instantaneous -> f_bar is a free parameter that happens to sit near 2/pi, the
      2.08% conflict can be absorbed into it, and the amplitude's decomposition loses
      one of its three derived factors.

  Recording which one is live therefore changes what the alpha_c conflict means, and
  the evidence points at the reading that makes the conflict REAL. That is the
  uncomfortable direction, which is the one worth trusting.

  STILL OWED. The operator form -- whether the shift in m_e is laid down as an integral
  over the winding epoch or read off the phase at recombination -- is a statement about
  the coupling that the corpus has not written down. The likelihood ratio argues for the
  first; it does not derive it.
